## Why 9 instead of 3?

| Metric | 3 commits | 9 commits |
|--------|-----------|-----------|
| Avg files/commit | 8.3 | 2.8 |
| Max files in one commit | 12 | 5 |
| Independently revertable? | ✗ (Commit 1 would break Commit 2) | ✓ Each is safe to revert |
| `git bisect` usable? | Hard — bugs hidden inside large commits | Easy — each commit is a working checkpoint |
| PR review experience | Reviewer must context-switch 4× per commit | One concern per commit, clear narrative |
| Cron job revert isolation | ✗ (bundled with home feed) | ✓ Single `git revert <sha>` |

